---
description: Service-layer rules for business logic in API services
globs: apps/api/services/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Service Layer

- Services must contain business rules, invariants, and cross-entity orchestration.
- Export service functions with explicit TypeScript input and return types.
- Service functions should return domain results or throw typed domain/app errors.

# Boundaries

- Services must not depend on HTTP primitives (`Request`, `Response`, headers, status codes).
- Services must not construct API response envelopes (`{ data }` / `{ error }`).
- Services must not import Node `fs`, database clients, or raw storage drivers directly.
- All persistence reads/writes must go through data/repository abstractions.

# Error And Validation Expectations

- Validate business constraints in services (uniqueness, ownership, state transitions).
- Treat route-level schema validation as precondition; re-check only business-critical assumptions.
- Do not swallow failures or return partial-success states without an explicit contract.
